Hello MARGARET,

We've redesigned wellsfargo.com to make it easier to bank from any device. As
part of the rollout, we are asking all online-banking customers to sign on
once between now and May 31, 2026 so we can:

  - migrate your saved transfers and bill-pay payees to the new layout;
  - verify the contact information used for security alerts;
  - reset your accessibility preferences (text size, contrast, audio).

Sign on at any time at:

  https://www.wellsfargo.com

If you do not sign on by May 31, 2026, your saved bill-pay payees will be
preserved but you will be asked to re-enter your contact details on your
next sign-on after that date. Your accounts and balances are not affected
and there is nothing else you need to do.

For your security:

  - Never sign on to your Wells Fargo account by clicking a link in an
    email. Type wellsfargo.com into your browser, or use the Wells Fargo
    Mobile app.
  - Wells Fargo will never ask for your password, PIN, or one-time access
    code by email, text, or phone.

If you have questions, sign on and message us, or call the number on the
back of your card.

